{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MsHu3w7toADqqALVtZoyBs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J9mMQiU1eBCBk3nHY2eCBZ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Method + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus areas are **Method** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"From Detection to Intervention: Structural Features for Real-Time LLM Agent Stagnation Monitoring\"\n\nThe paper addresses \"semantic stagnation\" in LLM agents — where agents emit plausible but unproductive actions. It proposes 30 lightweight structural features (<5ms/window) extracted from action logs, combined with a weak supervision pipeline (3 labeling functions aggregated via majority vote). Key claims:\n\n1. **Structural features dominate zero-shot cross-agent transfer**: 0.967 cross-agent F1 (SWE-Agent→OpenHands), +39.4pp over zero-shot neural probe, +21.5pp over best LLM judge.\n2. **LF temporal dynamics and label quality as transfer bottleneck**: Label quality (not model architecture) is the dominant transfer bottleneck. cmd_rep's contribution is coverage (-29.4pp when removed), not label precision.\n3. **Temporal label models: negative finding**: Three temporal label model variants (TWV, HMM-TLM, Lag-aware HMM) all fail to improve over simple majority vote.\n4. **Detection-to-intervention via early termination**: ~40% per-trajectory compute waste after stagnation onset; k=2 policy saves 24% compute preserving ~97% task success; Pareto AUC=0.84 vs oracle.\n\n## Method Details\n- 30 structural features in 3 groups: action-level (12), file-level (10), window-level dynamics (8)\n- Trajectory segmented into overlapping windows of k=5 consecutive actions\n- 3 labeling functions: cmd_rep (high precision command repetition), file_diff (minimal file changes), outcome_backpropagation (privileged, used in 3-LF only)\n- Labels aggregated via majority vote; conf≥2 means ≥2 LFs agree\n- Models: Gradient Boosted Trees (GB) and Random Forests (RF) trained on conf≥2 windows\n- Early termination: agent terminated when detector predicts stagnation for k consecutive windows\n\n## Experiment Setup\n- Training: SWE-Agent (5,000 trajectories on SWE-bench)\n- Evaluation: OpenHands (3,409 trajectories) — strict zero-shot cross-agent transfer\n- Baselines: GRU Probe (Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B), LLM Judge (Claude zero-shot and few-shot-CoT), Majority Vote, Oracle/Random\n- Metric: macro-F1 (stagnation prevalence ~19.3%)\n\n## Key Tables\n- Table 1: Matched-scope comparison — GB 0.993, GRU Probe fine-tuned 0.976, GRU Probe zero-shot 0.598\n- Table 2: LLM judge — Claude few-shot-CoT on OH: 0.752, Structural GB on OH: 0.967\n- Table 3: 2-LF vs 3-LF — RF conf≥2: 0.978 (-1.8pp), GB conf≥2: 0.872 (-12.0pp)\n- Table 4: Gold evaluation — SWE-only GB 0.877, TWV Probe 0.854, MV 0.798\n- Table 5: Compute waste — combined mean tail ratio 0.400, overall waste 11.1%\n- Table 6: Early termination sweep k=1..10 for 3-LF GB, 2-LF RF, Oracle, Random\n- Table 7: Pareto AUC — 3-LF GB 0.86, 2-LF RF 0.84, Oracle 0.97, Random 0.52\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nThe imagined experiments include:\n1. compute-waste-audit: SWE actual data, OH predicted. SWE 863/5000 trajectories have tails.\n2. early-termination-simulation: Cross-agent on OH conf≥2 windows. 3lf_gb and 2lf_rf sweeps.\n3. cost-effectiveness-pareto: Pareto frontier with 4 curves.\n4. 2lf-cross-agent: 2-LF deployable config results. RF 0.978 actual.\n5. matched-scope-eval: GB 0.993 vs probe zero-shot 0.598, delta 39.44pp. Actual.\n6. llm-on-oh: LLM judge on OH — PREDICTED (not actually executed).\n7. e4-gb-swe-gold: Gold set validation. GB SWE-only 0.877. Actual.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the paper focusing on:\n\n### Method Evaluation\n- Is the method well-motivated and technically sound?\n- Are the 30 structural features well-chosen? Any concerns about feature engineering?\n- Is the weak supervision pipeline (3 LFs + majority vote) appropriate?\n- Is the conf≥2 filtering well-justified?\n- Is the early termination policy (k-consecutive) reasonable?\n\n### Experiment Evaluation\n- Are the baselines fair and comprehensive?\n- Is the evaluation protocol rigorous (matched-scope, cross-agent)?\n- Are the statistical tests appropriate (bootstrap CI, p-values)?\n- Are there missing experiments or comparisons?\n- Check coverage: the review_context.yaml shows LLM-on-OH results are PREDICTED, not actual. Is this disclosed in the paper?\n- Is the gold set (N=505, 335 SWE-only) sufficient for the claims made?\n- The compute waste audit uses actual SWE data but predicted OH data — is this clear?\n\n### Specific Concerns to Address\n- Circularity: structural features trained on LF labels, tested on LF labels (silver). How well does the paper address this?\n- The 0.993 matched-scope F1 seems extremely high — any concern about information leakage or overfitting?\n- The probe zero-shot (0.598) uses Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B — is this a fair baseline or is a small/weak model being used to inflate the gap?\n- Early termination simulation is retrospective — how valid are the claims about deployment?\n\n### Output Format\nProvide your review in this format:\n\n**Summary**: 2-3 sentences on what the paper does.\n\n**Strengths** (S1-S5): Numbered list with brief justification.\n\n**Weaknesses** (W1-W5): Numbered list with brief justification. Flag severity (minor/moderate/major).\n\n**Questions for Authors**: 3-5 specific questions.\n\n**Method Soundness Score**: X/5\n\n**Experiment Rigor Score**: X/5\n\n**Overall Score**: X/6 (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept)\n\n**Confidence**: X/5\n","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21075,"cache_read_input_tokens":23704,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21075},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d074e59e-e78e-4d2c-a1a9-c5b03b4aa2ca","uuid":"6e126749-2e50-487f-97eb-3487ea735a45"}
