{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0114MQoAoqvvXdQzm75XSmEo","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/sections/method.tex:24:Compared to trajectory-level labeling, windows provide the granularity needed to pinpoint \\emph{when} stagnation begins and ends within a single task attempt, enabling downstream interventions such as early termination or strategy switching.\ndocs/paper/sections/limitations.tex:15:All results are offline; no intervention or real-time deployment evaluation has been conducted.\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:23:Our window-level formulation ($k{=}5$ consecutive actions, stride 1) captures short-range temporal patterns---such as repeated failures followed by strategy changes---that step-level approaches cannot express, while providing the granularity to pinpoint \\emph{when} stagnation begins and ends within a trajectory, enabling targeted interventions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014gVQX82GDH4gjf6y1yHnKj","session_id":"d074e59e-e78e-4d2c-a1a9-c5b03b4aa2ca","uuid":"642a82d1-02a3-4910-8a35-a68fc3f6efab","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:31:37.465Z"}
